The carrier needs a clear point of demarcation where their network ends and the customers network starts. 
This also demarks who is responsible to fix things, and where. 
A carrier or an Internet Service Provider (ISP) will install Customer Premises Equipment (CPE) as an active endpoint which they can test to. 
When we began designing WANs, the only available network was the TDM based telephony network. 
For technical reasons, this network was designed around 64 kbps channels and our original WAN technologies were the same.